WEBVTT

00:17:29.356 --> 00:17:31.396
the way they wanted
at those senior levels,

00:17:31.396 --> 00:17:34.436
because there was even more
pressure to behave in a certain way

00:17:34.436 --> 00:17:36.956
around what leadership
look like and style look like.

00:17:36.956 --> 00:17:38.996
And I think part
of the message of the book

00:17:38.996 --> 00:17:41.356
and part of what you're also
sharing in your story

00:17:41.396 --> 00:17:43.036
is we need to find power as we go

00:17:43.076 --> 00:17:46.396
and we need to remember and not think
it's something we'll find later.

00:17:46.396 --> 00:17:49.276
If you don't feel powerful
as you're rising in the structure,

00:17:49.316 --> 00:17:52.196
it's very unlikely you're going to
ultimately get to the seat

00:17:52.196 --> 00:17:53.396
and feel powerful,

00:17:53.396 --> 00:17:56.236
because you won't know how to find
and access your power.

00:17:56.236 --> 00:17:58.596
And your power comes
from inside and your history.

00:17:58.596 --> 00:18:00.796
S: The cognitive dissonance just grows.